    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0181" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW 1939/4–1044</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-10">10 April 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Reference is made to the
                    memorandum of Mr. James C. Dunn of April 8, 1944,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d182-f1"
                    /> transmitting the terms proposed by the Soviet Government for a Rumanian
                    armistice.</p>
                <p>The Joint Chiefs of Staff are of the opinion that our Government should give its
                    full assent to the military provisions of the proposed terms, the acceptance of
                    which by Rumania would result in the assumption by that nation of a
                    co-belligerent status with the Allies. <pb facs="0182" n="172" xml:id="pg172"/>
                    Such action by Rumania would be an event of such cardinal importance in the
                    further prosecution of the war that it is hoped that our Government may find a
                    basis for agreement with the Soviet and British Governments on any nonmilitary
                    provisions of the proposed terms.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d182-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Joint Chiefs of Staff: <lb/>
                    <signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chief of Staff, U.S. Army</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d182-f1" n="55" xml:id="d182-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d182-f2" n="56" xml:id="d182-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 3469, April 29, 10 p.m., to London, the Department stated that the
                    revised views of the Joint Chiefs of Staff as set forth in Eacom 16,
                    Department’s 2815 of April 10, 6 p.m. (<ref target="frus1944v01#pg_210">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 210</ref>), should be taken into
                    account as applying also to surrender terms for the satellite states (740.00119
                    EAC/184a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
